":"independence","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"atzma'ut"},{"he":"מדינה","en":"state","alt":["country"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"medinah"},{"he":"הכרזה","en":"declaration","alt":["announcement"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"hakrazah"},{"he":"שואה","en":"Holocaust","alt":["catastrophe"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"sho'ah"},{"he":"ציונות","en":"Zionism","alt":[],"from":"lexicon","tr":"tziyonut"},{"he":"כיבוש","en":"conquest","alt":["occupation"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"kibush"},{"he":"שלום","en":"peace","alt":["hello"],"from":"lexicon","tr":"shalom"},{"he":"היסטוריה","en":"history","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"historiyah"},{"he":"היסטורי","en":"historic","alt":["historical"],"from":"skill","tr":"histori"},{"he":"הסכם","en":"agreement","alt":["accord"],"from":"skill","tr":"heskem"},{"he":"קורבנות","en":"victims","alt":["sacrifices"],"from":"skill","tr":"korbanot"},{"he":"הקמת","en":"establishment of","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"hakamat"},{"he":"נלחמה","en":"fought","alt":[],"from":"skill","tr":"nilkhamah"},{"he":"חוקרת","en":"researches","alt":["investigates"],"from":"skill","tr":"khokeret"},{"he":"תנועה","en":"movement","alt":[],"from":"phrase","tr":"tnu'ah"},{"he":"לאומית","en":"national","alt":[],"from":"phrase","tr":"le'umit"},{"he":"מדינת","en":"state of","alt":[],"from":"phrase","tr":"medinat"},{"he":"הכריזה","en":"declared","alt":["announced"],"from":"phrase","tr":"hikhrizah"},{"he":"אסון","en":"disaster","alt":["catastrophe"],"from":"phrase","tr":"ason"},{"he":"כולם","en":"everyone","alt":["everybody"],"from":"phrase","tr":"kulam"}],"lexemes":["מלחמה","המלחמה","במלחמה","עצמאות","העצמאות","מדינה","המדינה","מדינת","הכרזה","ההכרזה","שואה","השואה","ציונות","הציונות","כיבוש","הכיבוש","שלום","השלום","היסטוריה","ההיסטוריה","מההיסטוריה","היסטורי","הסכם","קורבנות","הקמת","נלחמה","לחמו","תנועה","לאומית","חוקרת","חוגגת","הוקמה","השפיעה","הביאה","שינתה","נקראה","הכריז","הכריזה","זוכרים","עולמי","אסון"],"tips":"## Key Events in Israeli and Jewish History\n\nHere are some important terms and dates:\n\n- **הכרזת העצמאות** (Declaration of Independence) — May 14, 1948\n- **מלחמת העצמאות** (War of Independence) — 1948-1949\n- **השואה** (The Holocaust) — 1939-1945\n- **הציונות** (Zionism) — A national movement for the return of the Jewish people to their homeland, beginning in the late 19th century\n\n### The Construct State (סמיכות)\n\nMany history words use the **construct state**, where two nouns combine:\n\n| Base form | Construct form | Example |\n|---|---|---|\n| מדינה (state) | מדינ**ת** | מדינ**ת** ישראל (State of Israel) |\n| מלחמה (war) | מלחמ**ת** | מלחמ**ת** העצמאות (War of Independence) |\n| הכרזה (declaration) | הכרז**ת** | הכרז**ת** העצמאות (Declaration of Independence) |\n\nNotice how feminine nouns ending in **ה-** change to **ת-** in construct form.\n\n### Passive Voice (נפעל)\n\nSeveral sentences use the **נפעל** (Nif'al) pattern for passive:\n- הוקמה — was established (from הקים)\n- נקראה — was read / was called (from קרא)\n- נלחמה — fought (reflexive, from לחם)"}